WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:02.081
- Hey Andrew, how's it goin'?

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:02.914
What's up man?

00:00:02.914 --> 00:00:05.797
My bestie, Keith, actually,
is not available right now,

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:07.705
but I was wondering if you would be

00:00:07.705 --> 00:00:10.045
at all willing to come with
me on a food adventure?

00:00:10.045 --> 00:00:11.358
- So I'm just like your backup?

00:00:11.358 --> 00:00:13.600
- Um, We're doin' pizza.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:14.433
- Okay.

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:15.365
- Sweet!
- Let's go.

00:00:15.365 --> 00:00:16.541
(whooshing)

00:00:16.541 --> 00:00:17.769
(funky brass music)

00:00:17.769 --> 00:00:18.727
- So where are we going?

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.560
- We are on our way, right now,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.402
to eat three different pizzas at three

00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:23.250
drastically different price points.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.516
And we're gonna find out which one

00:00:24.516 --> 00:00:26.130
is the most worth-it at its price.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.322
- What does the expensive one cost?

00:00:27.322 --> 00:00:28.951
- 135 dollars.

00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:31.110
- 135 dollars, is it made of gold?

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.587
Why do you need me to come with you?

00:00:32.587 --> 00:00:34.416
- Because, I need a partner in crime,

00:00:34.416 --> 00:00:36.115
and you are the best friend today.

00:00:36.115 --> 00:00:37.618
- Lemme look up some dynamic duos

00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:39.416
and then we can decide which one we are.

00:00:39.416 --> 00:00:41.362
Mickey Mouse, Minnie Mouse, Who's who?

00:00:41.362 --> 00:00:42.768
- Why can't we just be Steven and Andrew?

00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:44.725
- Spaghetti and meatballs,
milk and cookies.

00:00:44.725 --> 00:00:45.558
- I'll meet you inside.

00:00:45.558 --> 00:00:46.391
- Beavis and Butthead.

00:00:46.391 --> 00:00:47.903
Mary Kate and Ashley Olson.

00:00:47.903 --> 00:00:50.236
I think it's pretty obvious.

00:00:52.066 --> 00:00:56.223
(driving percussive music)

00:00:56.223 --> 00:00:57.229
- We're gonna serve for you, today,

00:00:57.229 --> 00:00:59.284
our basic pizza. It's our Simple Pie.

00:00:59.284 --> 00:01:01.129
Our Simple Pie is just
tomato sauce, Parmesan,

00:01:01.129 --> 00:01:02.508
and a whole milk mozzarella.

00:01:02.508 --> 00:01:03.745
As well as our Green Stripe.

00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:05.591
It's got basil pesto, mozzarella,

00:01:05.591 --> 00:01:07.374
all-natural chicken, wild baby arugula,

00:01:07.374 --> 00:01:08.832
and roasted red bell peppers.

00:01:08.832 --> 00:01:09.678
- [Steven] How much is the Simple Pie?

00:01:09.678 --> 00:01:11.981
- [Brad] At this location it's
five dollars and 25 cents.

00:01:11.981 --> 00:01:12.987
- [Steven] That's value, right there.

00:01:12.987 --> 00:01:14.355
- [Brad] Or for 7.95 you can get

00:01:14.355 --> 00:01:16.068
as many toppings as you like,
as much of them as you like.

00:01:16.068 --> 00:01:17.026
- That's pretty great.

00:01:17.026 --> 00:01:17.974
- And here's the cool thing about it.

00:01:17.974 --> 00:01:19.513
Just like any fine dining restaurant,

00:01:19.513 --> 00:01:20.790
all of our stuff's all-natural

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.200
- So like, how many pies does
this location make in a day?

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.381
- We've done over 1,200.

00:01:24.381 --> 00:01:25.875
- That's a lot of pizza!

00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:28.005
- [Steven] We're here. The
first pizza restaurant.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:30.427
- Not how I thought my
day would go but, alright.

00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:31.463
- This pizza's the size of your head,

00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:32.999
and it's five dollars, can we cheers?

00:01:32.999 --> 00:01:34.401
It's really thin.
- With the pizza?

00:01:34.401 --> 00:01:35.234
- Yeah.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:36.067
- Like,

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:38.008
(funky bass music)

00:01:38.008 --> 00:01:38.960
(laughing)

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:40.263
(funky bass music)

00:01:40.263 --> 00:01:41.550
- Yeah, it's a great pizza.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.757
- This pizza's called the Simple Pie.

00:01:42.757 --> 00:01:44.259
It's very simple, and I think that's

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:45.499
how you should do things in life.

00:01:45.499 --> 00:01:46.792
- Five dollars you're getting the

00:01:46.792 --> 00:01:48.272
three things that make pizza, pizza.

00:01:48.272 --> 00:01:50.112
- You have good dough.
You have good sauce.

00:01:50.112 --> 00:01:51.027
You have good cheese.

00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:54.733
- This sauce is delicious.
Have you had this sauce yet?

00:01:54.733 --> 00:01:55.932
- I've been eating the pizza.

00:01:55.932 --> 00:01:57.208
Alright let's try the other pizza now.

00:01:57.208 --> 00:01:59.440
So we got the most expensive
pizza here, and it's $7.95.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:00.390
(excited gasping)

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:01.223
Cheers.

00:02:01.223 --> 00:02:02.083
(crunching)

00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:04.225
This one is very good. You demolish pizza.

00:02:04.225 --> 00:02:05.626
- I know, this is something that you're

00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:08.020
gonna have to get used to.
I have no self-control.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.569
- You are a pizza monster.

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:11.756
- And you are a pizza plebeian.

00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:12.589
- That's pretty good.

00:02:12.589 --> 00:02:13.422
- Next place.

00:02:13.422 --> 00:02:14.355
- That Simple Pie was great, but I would

00:02:14.355 --> 00:02:17.118
spend the extra three dollars
to get that pesto pizza.

00:02:17.118 --> 00:02:19.840
- I think I would just get
two simple pies instead.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:20.917
(cymbals crashing)

00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:22.605
- No, that's not how it works!

00:02:22.605 --> 00:02:24.287
I say the pizza fact!
(horn blasting)

00:02:24.287 --> 00:02:25.120
- Pizza fact!

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:25.953
(cymbals crashing)

00:02:25.953 --> 00:02:26.786
I like pizza.

00:02:26.786 --> 00:02:27.619
Pizza fact.

00:02:27.619 --> 00:02:30.520
Experts theorize that the price of pizza

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.190
in New York City will always equal

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.990
the price of a subway fare.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:36.422
- So if you have a slice of pizza,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.536
you could trade that for a free ride

00:02:38.536 --> 00:02:39.369
(groaning)

00:02:39.369 --> 00:02:40.478
- I've had too much pizza today.

00:02:40.478 --> 00:02:42.038
- We've only been to one place.

00:02:42.038 --> 00:02:43.945
- You want a Tootsie Pop?

00:02:43.945 --> 00:02:45.061
(suckers rattling)

00:02:45.061 --> 00:02:46.710
(car humming)

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:47.543
(popping)

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:50.626
(funky guitar music)

00:02:51.862 --> 00:02:53.390
- We're gonna make a
buratta pizza for you today.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.039
Buratta cheese is basically a
fresh mozzarella preparation.

00:02:56.039 --> 00:02:58.773
Very soft, rich, luxurious
mozzarella cheese.

00:02:58.773 --> 00:02:59.916
First we'll stretch the dough,

00:02:59.916 --> 00:03:01.283
and then we'll put a little bit

00:03:01.283 --> 00:03:02.506
of olive oil on the crust.

00:03:02.506 --> 00:03:03.702
We'll top it with our pizzato,

00:03:03.702 --> 00:03:05.438
which is our tomato sauce, and then layer

00:03:05.438 --> 00:03:07.095
the squash blossoms over the top.

00:03:07.095 --> 00:03:09.029
Spread it over the pizza,
it goes in the oven.

00:03:09.029 --> 00:03:10.127
- [Steven] And how do you
know when it's finished?

00:03:10.127 --> 00:03:12.621
- One of the true tells is
you turn it up on one end,

00:03:12.621 --> 00:03:14.574
and it will stay like a board.

00:03:14.574 --> 00:03:16.291
And then it gets topped
with the buratta cheese,

00:03:16.291 --> 00:03:17.653
a little bit of extra virgin olive oil,

00:03:17.653 --> 00:03:19.130
sea salt, and black pepper.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:19.963
- [Andrew] It sounds delicious.

00:03:19.963 --> 00:03:22.526
- [Steven] What makes you pizza
different from other pizzas?

00:03:22.526 --> 00:03:24.281
- We focus, a lot, on the crust.

00:03:24.281 --> 00:03:25.506
The toppings are important, and we put

00:03:25.506 --> 00:03:26.908
a lot of attention to that,

00:03:26.908 --> 00:03:28.674
but people don't know that that's

00:03:28.674 --> 00:03:29.896
what makes a pizza so good.

00:03:29.896 --> 00:03:31.373
They just think it's the toppings,

00:03:31.373 --> 00:03:32.776
but it's actually the crust.

00:03:32.776 --> 00:03:34.380
(gentle piano music)

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.024
(lips smacking)

00:03:36.024 --> 00:03:37.437
- Oh wow, that is so good.

00:03:37.437 --> 00:03:40.110
This pizza comes in quarters.
I think that is awesome.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:41.585
- These are all good slices.

00:03:41.585 --> 00:03:43.018
Cheers.

00:03:43.018 --> 00:03:43.912
(tsking)

00:03:43.912 --> 00:03:44.812
Cheers.

00:03:44.812 --> 00:03:46.892
(calm violin music)

00:03:46.892 --> 00:03:47.725
(satisfied grunting)

00:03:47.725 --> 00:03:48.568
- That's a perfect pizza.

00:03:48.568 --> 00:03:49.401
- I'm calling it right now,

00:03:49.401 --> 00:03:50.910
we're not gonna get a
better pizza than this.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.626
(crunching)

00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:55.076
I just got into the crust.

00:03:55.076 --> 00:03:57.348
The way that really fresh popcorn tastes,

00:03:57.348 --> 00:03:59.632
we got like, flavored air
comin' out of the crust.

00:03:59.632 --> 00:04:00.803
How are you not excited about this?

00:04:00.803 --> 00:04:02.286
(crunching)

00:04:02.286 --> 00:04:03.119
Do you get what I'm talkin' about?

00:04:03.119 --> 00:04:03.952
- Whoa!

00:04:03.952 --> 00:04:05.509
You know what's also
interesting? The pepper.

00:04:05.509 --> 00:04:08.129
- Yes. I love putting
black pepper on stuff.

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:09.696
I put a disgusting amount on it.

00:04:09.696 --> 00:04:10.529
- This is a lot
- My girlfriend

00:04:10.529 --> 00:04:11.362
yells at me all the time.

00:04:11.362 --> 00:04:12.870
- You have a girlfriend?

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:14.448
Feels like I'm eating something

00:04:14.448 --> 00:04:17.523
that was prepared with love, for me,

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.681
and you, and you, and all
of you guys out there.

00:04:20.681 --> 00:04:21.535
Are you havin' a great time?

00:04:21.535 --> 00:04:24.217
- Pizzeria Mozza, amazing, 10 outta 10.

00:04:24.217 --> 00:04:26.730
Steven Lim, pretty fun.

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:30.050
I feel like I'm starting
to get drunk off pizza.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:31.625
- Where did he get that pizza?

00:04:31.625 --> 00:04:32.666
Pizza fact!

00:04:32.666 --> 00:04:34.754
Did you know, that in 2001,

00:04:34.754 --> 00:04:37.212
Pizza Hut delivered a pizza to

00:04:37.212 --> 00:04:38.830
the International Space Station?

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:40.073
Can you imagine eating pizza in space?

00:04:40.073 --> 00:04:42.331
- Then I'd be pissed off
that they sent me Pizza Hut.

00:04:42.331 --> 00:04:43.896
- Pizza Hut's good, what
are you talking about?

00:04:43.896 --> 00:04:46.137
- If you're sending it
all the way to space,

00:04:46.137 --> 00:04:47.595
they could go ahead and send you

00:04:47.595 --> 00:04:48.973
the best pizza from Earth.

00:04:48.973 --> 00:04:52.095
- What will it take for
the next pizza to win out?

00:04:52.095 --> 00:04:55.426
(harmonized singing)

00:04:55.426 --> 00:04:56.259
- I dunno.

00:04:56.259 --> 00:04:59.426
(gentle violin music)

00:05:02.325 --> 00:05:04.300
- I'm the chef de cuisine
at Spago, Beverly Hills.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.351
I will be making Italian
white truffle pizza.

00:05:06.351 --> 00:05:07.618
That's in season right now.

00:05:07.618 --> 00:05:09.150
What's so special is the truffle.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:11.703
Truffles are fungus and
they grow under the ground.

00:05:11.703 --> 00:05:15.853
A pound of white truffle will
go as high as 3,000 dollars.

00:05:15.853 --> 00:05:19.199
So a little piece like
this, about 100 dollars.

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:20.828
We will be stretching this dough

00:05:20.828 --> 00:05:22.942
to about nine inch diameter.

00:05:22.942 --> 00:05:24.844
We'll put mozzarella on top of the dough.

00:05:24.844 --> 00:05:26.552
The dough will go in the pizza oven

00:05:26.552 --> 00:05:30.861
for about five minutes. We
use real wood fired oven.

00:05:30.861 --> 00:05:33.695
This will give, somewhat, a smoky aroma.

00:05:33.695 --> 00:05:35.198
Once it comes out, we're going

00:05:35.198 --> 00:05:37.189
to shave a lot of white truffle on it.

00:05:37.189 --> 00:05:38.022
- That's it?

00:05:38.022 --> 00:05:38.972
- That's it.

00:05:38.972 --> 00:05:39.805
- Three ingredients?

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.651
- As soon as you shave
the white truffle on it,

00:05:41.651 --> 00:05:43.468
the aroma will just explode.

00:05:43.468 --> 00:05:45.620
It has it's own distinct aroma,

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.339
you can't find it in anything else.

00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:49.652
This is 135 dollars on the menu.

00:05:49.652 --> 00:05:51.475
Actually a bargain.

00:05:51.475 --> 00:05:53.708
When we have a special
ingredient like this,

00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:56.015
